FidelityFX Super Resolution 1.0 (FSR 1) - pristine upstream reference copy
==========================================================================

Source:  https://github.com/GPUOpen-Effects/FidelityFX-FSR
Commit:  a21ffb8f6c13233ba336352bdff293894c706575  (branch master, retrieved 2026-09-13)
Files:   license.txt      (verbatim from repo root)
         ffx_a.h          (verbatim from ffx-fsr/ffx_a.h)
         ffx_fsr1.h       (verbatim from ffx-fsr/ffx_fsr1.h)

License: MIT (see license.txt). Copyright (c) 2021 Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.
         ffx_a.h also carries a second MIT notice crediting Michal Drobot (c) 2014
         for concepts used in its FLOAT APPROXIMATIONS section.

These headers are NOT compiled. shaders.cmake only stringifies renderergl2/glsl/*.glsl,
so nothing here is built into the dll. They are kept as the reference the trimmed GLSL
ports were derived from, and to carry the upstream license verbatim.

The compiled ports live in renderergl2/glsl/:
  fsr_easu_fp.glsl       - EASU spatial upscale (FSR_EASU_F 32-bit float path)
  fsr_rcas_fp.glsl       - RCAS sharpen (FSR_RCAS_F 32-bit float path, DENOISE on)
  fsr_downscale_fp.glsl  - HZM SSAA tent downsample (not FSR; used at render scale > 1)

Port notes:
  - 32-bit float path only (no A_HALF / float16 / Vulkan-GLSL types).
  - Constants (FsrEasuCon / FsrRcasCon) are computed on the CPU in
    renderergl2/tr_postprocess.c and passed as plain vec4 floats (u_FsrCon0..3);
    the upstream uint bit-reinterpret (AU1_AF1 / AF4_AU4) is not used.
  - The bit-hack rcp / rsqrt approximations (APrxLoRcpF1 etc.) are replaced by exact
    GLSL (1.0/x, inversesqrt) on the 32-bit float path.
  - EASU textureGather requires GLSL 4.00 or GL_ARB_gpu_shader5; the port declares
    the extension and the renderer falls back to a bilinear blit if EASU fails to build.

Binary distribution: the MIT notice in license.txt must ship with any binary that
embeds these shaders (the compiled renderer_opengl2.dll does). Add it to the release
third-party notices.
